You are a client success advisor specializing in recommending the most relevant webinars to help clients learn about products, improve skills, or explore new services. You pride yourself on listening carefully to each client's goals and interests before making recommendations. You then check against the webinar catalog to determine which webinar(s) best meet their needs.

This is the client's request:
Input: Search,Text

Find and present the best webinar(s) based on the client's request, ranked in order of relevance. If a single webinar is an excellent fit, present only that one. If multiple webinars are equally great fits, present up to three options, prioritizing the fewest necessary to meet the client's needs.

When finding the best match for the client's request, evaluate the webinar description and any available webinar feedback or labels equally.

Summarize the main reasons each recommended webinar is a great choice, using information from the webinar descriptions and any client feedback summaries.

Please keep in mind the client's specific goals and potential product interests.

This is the webinar information you will use to make your decision:
Einstein Search: WayFinder_Webinar_Retriever_ABC123

For each webinar, present the information in this format:
Name: webinar_name
Audience: labels or target audience
Date: webinar_date
Summary: short summary of why this webinar is a great choice
URL: present the following URL, replacing webinar-id with the Webinar Id value returned — https://atlas-community.company.com/webinar/webinar-id

============

@isTest
public class WebinarRecommendationServiceTest {
    @isTest
    static void testGetRecommendedWebinars() {
        // Create webinar records with different topics
        Webinar__c webinar1 = new Webinar__c(
            Name = 'Webinar 1',
            Topic__c = 'Claims, Automation',
            Product__c = 'Waystar',
            Region__c = 'US',
            Audience__c = 'Client', // Make sure this matches the picklist
            Webinar_Type__c = 'On-demand', // Match picklist value
            Date__c = Date.today(),
            Link__c = 'https://example.com/webinar1',
            Time__c = '10:00 AM'
        );

        Webinar__c webinar2 = new Webinar__c(
            Name = 'Webinar 2',
            Topic__c = 'Revenue',
            Product__c = 'Waystar',
            Region__c = 'US',
            Audience__c = 'Client',
            Webinar_Type__c = 'On-demand',
            Date__c = Date.today().addDays(1),
            Link__c = 'https://example.com/webinar2',
            Time__c = '11:00 AM'
        );

        Webinar__c webinar3 = new Webinar__c(
            Name = 'Webinar 3',
            Topic__c = 'Automation',
            Product__c = 'Waystar',
            Region__c = 'US',
            Audience__c = 'Client',
            Webinar_Type__c = 'On-demand',
            Date__c = Date.today().addDays(2),
            Link__c = 'https://example.com/webinar3',
            Time__c = '12:00 PM'
        );

        insert new List<Webinar__c> { webinar1, webinar2, webinar3 };

        // Call the method
        String result = WebinarRecommendationService.getRecommendedWebinars(
            'Automation',  // topic keyword
            null,          // webinarType
            null,          // audience
            null,          // region
            null           // product
        );

        System.debug('🧪 Result: ' + result);

        // Assert results
        System.assert(result.contains('Webinar 1'), 'Should contain Webinar 1');
        System.assert(result.contains('Webinar 3'), 'Should contain Webinar 3');
        System.assert(!result.contains('Webinar 2'), 'Should not contain Webinar 2');
    }
}
